WEBVTT

1
00:00:29.958 --> 00:00:36.541
<b>An opportunity to make a significant contribution</b>

2
00:00:36.541 --> 00:00:40.375
<b>For a Kshatriya like Arjun,</b>

3
00:00:40.375 --> 00:00:42.375
<b>a gateway to heaven.</b>

4
00:00:42.375 --> 00:00:43.541
<b>But</b>

5
00:00:43.541 --> 00:00:49.583
<b>this can only happen when he agrees</b>

6
00:00:49.583 --> 00:00:54.000
<b>What if Arjun refuses to fight this war?</b>

7
00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:56.875
<b>Here Krishna explains exactly that.</b>

8
00:00:56.875 --> 00:00:58.666
<b>He tells Arjun</b>

9
00:00:58.666 --> 00:01:02.250
<b>that if you don't fight this righteous war,</b>

10
00:01:02.250 --> 00:01:05.500
<b>not only will you lose your honor,</b>

11
00:01:05.500 --> 00:01:09.541
<b>but by failing to follow your inherent dharma,</b>

12
00:01:09.541 --> 00:01:12.166
<b>you will also incur sin.</b>

13
00:01:17.291 --> 00:01:21.000
<b>Krishna is making Arjun aware</b>

14
00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:23.166
<b>He says: You are a Kshatriya,</b>

15
00:01:23.166 --> 00:01:25.958
<b>and your glory lies in warfare.</b>

16
00:01:25.958 --> 00:01:26.833
<b>But</b>

17
00:01:26.833 --> 00:01:29.625
<b>if you turn your back like this,</b>

18
00:01:29.625 --> 00:01:31.458
<b>if you abandon your weapons thus,</b>

19
00:01:31.458 --> 00:01:33.416
<b>it's a matter of disgrace</b>

20
00:01:33.416 --> 00:01:38.208
<b>all the honor you've earned until now</b>

21
00:01:38.208 --> 00:01:39.208
<b>And secondly,</b>

22
00:01:39.208 --> 00:01:44.041
<b>being a Kshatriya, participating</b>

23
00:01:44.041 --> 00:01:49.291
<b>And if you neglect this dharma,</b>

24
00:01:49.291 --> 00:01:51.041
<b>Arjun's agony</b>

25
00:01:51.041 --> 00:01:52.833
<b>was that if he fought this war,</b>

26
00:01:52.833 --> 00:01:56.250
<b>the sin of his kinsmen's death</b>

27
00:01:56.250 --> 00:02:02.625
<b>Here Krishna is resolving Arjun's dilemma,</b>

28
00:02:02.625 --> 00:02:06.000
<b>He is clarifying that you're thinking wrongly</b>

29
00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:08.458
<b>no sin will accrue from fighting this war.</b>

30
00:02:08.458 --> 00:02:09.166
<b>Yes,</b>

31
00:02:09.166 --> 00:02:11.416
<b>if you abandon it,</b>

32
00:02:11.416 --> 00:02:14.291
<b>you will certainly invite sin.</b>

33
00:02:18.791 --> 00:02:23.958
<b>There must have been a time in your life too</b>

34
00:02:23.958 --> 00:02:26.000
<b>when you felt like enough!</b>

35
00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:33.958
<b>Let's just abandon all responsibilities and</b>

36
00:02:33.958 --> 00:02:37.000
<b>What did you do at such times?</b>

37
00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:38.083
<b>Especially</b>

38
00:02:38.083 --> 00:02:41.916
<b>when one becomes mentally overwhelmed,</b>

39
00:02:41.916 --> 00:02:44.916
<b>such thoughts are natural.</b>

40
00:02:44.916 --> 00:02:47.083
<b>Stress is natural.</b>

41
00:02:47.083 --> 00:02:47.833
<b>But</b>

42
00:02:47.833 --> 00:02:52.500
<b>making such important decisions under stress</b>

43
00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:54.708
<b>isn't right.</b>

44
00:02:54.708 --> 00:03:00.750
<b>Yet it's also not right to live</b>

45
00:03:00.750 --> 00:03:03.583
<b>So what should be done?</b>

46
00:03:03.583 --> 00:03:04.875
<b>Usually,</b>

47
00:03:04.875 --> 00:03:07.666
<b>such situations are temporary,</b>

48
00:03:07.666 --> 00:03:09.500
<b>so don't be disturbed.</b>

49
00:03:09.500 --> 00:03:15.708
<b>If you've made it through before,</b>

50
00:03:15.708 --> 00:03:17.625
<b>Then, with a calm mind,</b>

51
00:03:17.625 --> 00:03:21.708
<b>ask yourself these questions:</b>

52
00:03:21.708 --> 00:03:25.500
<b>You've endured such anxiety before.</b>

53
00:03:25.500 --> 00:03:27.541
<b>That time too passed.</b>

54
00:03:27.541 --> 00:03:30.500
<b>So what's so different this time</b>

55
00:03:30.500 --> 00:03:34.791
<b>that abandoning responsibilities seems</b>

56
00:03:34.791 --> 00:03:35.875
<b>What will happen</b>

57
00:03:35.875 --> 00:03:41.125
<b>if you ultimately abandon your responsibilities?</b>

58
00:03:41.125 --> 00:03:47.500
<b>What impact will this have</b>

59
00:03:47.500 --> 00:03:50.250
<b>Even knowing all this,</b>

60
00:03:50.250 --> 00:03:55.041
<b>if you run away from the situation,</b>

61
00:03:55.041 --> 00:03:57.833
<b>will you find peace?</b>

62
00:03:57.833 --> 00:04:01.791
<b>These questions will surely lead</b>

63
00:04:01.791 --> 00:04:04.000
<b>which most often will be</b>

64
00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:09.916
<b>that this very thought of abandoning</b>

65
00:04:09.916 --> 00:04:17.291
<b>You've handled countless dilemmas</b>

66
00:04:17.291 --> 00:04:20.166
<b>This is nothing new.</b>

67
00:04:20.166 --> 00:04:25.083
<b>Fulfill your duties with confidence and courage.</b>

68
00:04:25.083 --> 00:04:31.083
<b>You possess complete capability</b>

69
00:04:35.541 --> 00:04:43.541
<b>All parents want their children to only love them.</b>

70
00:04:43.541 --> 00:04:47.166
<b>To never think ill of them.</b>

71
00:04:47.166 --> 00:04:48.625
<b>But</b>

72
00:04:48.625 --> 00:04:52.458
<b>sometimes this desire becomes so strong</b>

73
00:04:52.458 --> 00:04:57.250
<b>that it leads parents astray from their duty.</b>

74
00:04:57.250 --> 00:04:59.958
<b>Fearing their children might feel hurt,</b>

75
00:04:59.958 --> 00:05:11.000
<b>they overlook and stay silent even when</b>

76
00:05:11.000 --> 00:05:13.333
<b>Only praise for good deeds,</b>

77
00:05:13.333 --> 00:05:20.291
<b>and only silence for wrongdoings.</b>

78
00:05:20.291 --> 00:05:25.250
<b>Dhritarashtra did exactly this.</b>

79
00:05:25.250 --> 00:05:26.375
<b>And then</b>

80
00:05:26.375 --> 00:05:29.916
<b>as children grow older,</b>

81
00:05:29.916 --> 00:05:33.625
<b>their nature becomes more stubborn.</b>

82
00:05:33.625 --> 00:05:34.833
<b>And if they</b>

83
00:05:34.833 --> 00:05:38.291
<b>proceed down a wrong path</b>

84
00:05:38.291 --> 00:05:41.083
<b>if they spoil their life,</b>

85
00:05:41.083 --> 00:05:45.833
<b>nothing remains except regret.</b>

86
00:05:45.833 --> 00:05:51.333
<b>Society too holds parents responsible</b>

87
00:05:51.333 --> 00:05:52.208
<b>Because</b>

88
00:05:52.208 --> 00:05:54.041
<b>isn't this the truth</b>

89
00:05:54.041 --> 00:06:00.375
<b>that it's the parents' duty to raise their</b>

90
00:06:00.375 --> 00:06:02.333
<b>And not just this,</b>

91
00:06:02.333 --> 00:06:13.708
<b>even those children blame their parents for</b>

92
00:06:13.708 --> 00:06:16.833
<b>So what was gained in the end?</b>

93
00:06:16.833 --> 00:06:21.791
<b>Contempt from both society and children.</b>

94
00:06:21.791 --> 00:06:28.041
<b>This is the consequence</b>

95
00:06:28.041 --> 00:06:31.875
<b>Praise for good deeds is necessary,</b>

96
00:06:31.875 --> 00:06:32.750
<b>but</b>

97
00:06:32.750 --> 00:06:41.333
<b>guidance for wrong actions, and sometimes</b>

98
00:06:41.333 --> 00:06:44.416
<b>This is for your children's welfare,</b>

99
00:06:44.416 --> 00:06:49.041
<b>whose complete responsibility lies with you.</b>

100
00:06:53.500 --> 00:06:55.041
<b>In the workplace,</b>

101
00:06:55.041 --> 00:06:57.041
<b>your evaluation</b>

102
00:06:57.041 --> 00:07:01.500
<b>doesn't depend solely on your expertise.</b>

103
00:07:01.500 --> 00:07:05.583
<b>Your attitude towards given responsibilities</b>

104
00:07:05.583 --> 00:07:11.083
<b>also has a profound impact on this assessment.</b>

105
00:07:11.083 --> 00:07:16.458
<b>If the attitude is right,</b>

106
00:07:16.458 --> 00:07:17.333
<b>But</b>

107
00:07:17.333 --> 00:07:19.583
<b>if the attitude itself isn't correct,</b>

108
00:07:19.583 --> 00:07:25.000
<b>if you're consistently unable</b>

109
00:07:25.000 --> 00:07:27.166
<b>if you run from them,</b>

110
00:07:27.166 --> 00:07:31.916
<b>then even skillfulness becomes worthless.</b>

111
00:07:31.916 --> 00:07:38.000
<b>In such situations, your colleagues</b>

112
00:07:38.000 --> 00:07:41.458
<b>they view you with distrust.</b>

113
00:07:41.458 --> 00:07:45.083
<b>And if this continues,</b>

114
00:07:45.083 --> 00:07:52.416
<b>they gradually stop giving you</b>

115
00:07:52.416 --> 00:07:54.125
<b>You know</b>

116
00:07:54.125 --> 00:07:58.083
<b>what impact this can have.</b>

117
00:07:58.083 --> 00:08:01.375
<b>Your progress may halt,</b>

118
00:08:01.375 --> 00:08:08.375
<b>and perhaps it may even lead to termination.</b>

119
00:08:08.375 --> 00:08:12.000
<b>These 3 things are extremely essential:</b>

120
00:08:12.000 --> 00:08:16.458
<b>Maintain a positive attitude towards work</b>

121
00:08:16.458 --> 00:08:19.583
<b>Don't avoid your responsibilities</b>

122
00:08:19.583 --> 00:08:24.458
<b>When a difficult situation arises, don't run from it</b>

123
00:08:24.458 --> 00:08:30.708
<b>seek help from someone experienced,</b>

124
00:08:30.708 --> 00:08:32.791
<b>When you do this,</b>

125
00:08:32.791 --> 00:08:36.166
<b>not only will your work efficiency increase,</b>

126
00:08:36.166 --> 00:08:37.000
<b>but</b>

127
00:08:37.000 --> 00:08:40.541
<b>people's trust in you will grow as well.</b>

128
00:08:40.541 --> 00:08:46.791
<b>This is crucial for progress and success</b>

